{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QGK7gBnNtJNfF3TgUN4nHC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# R87 — Tests/Docs review — Phase 11 hardening + documentation completeness\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** Review for Phase 11\n4\t**Type:** review\n5\t**Model class:** advanced\n6\t**Depends on:** T80, T81, T82, T83, T84, T85, T86\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Documentation Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#documentation-requirements), [§Testing Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#testing-requirements)\n8\t**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); definition-of-done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`).\n9\t\n10\t## Purpose\n11\t\n12\tThis review certifies that Phase 11 has delivered the complete hardening test suite (large-repo, concurrency, recovery, corruption, partial-index, workspace-boundary, migration, MCP compat) and the complete documentation suite (eleven required docs plus runbook plus recovery playbook). It is the gate that R88 (definition-of-done) and R89 (final readiness) depend on: a missing test family or a missing doc would force later gates to either block or accept a deferral, both of which violate the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Passing this review means the system is documented and proven production-grade per spec §Phase 11 DoD.\n13\t\n14\t## Inputs to read\n15\t\n16\t- Every artifact produced by T80–T86:\n17\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/large_repo_tests.rs`\n18\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/concurrency_tests.rs`\n19\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/recovery_tests.rs`\n20\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/corruption_tests.rs`\n21\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/partial_index_tests.rs`\n22\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/workspace_boundary_tests.rs`\n23\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/migration_tests.rs`\n24\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs`\n25\t  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/large_repo_results.json`\n26\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`\n27\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`\n28\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`\n29\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`\n30\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`\n31\t  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`\n32\t  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`\n33\t  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`\n34\t  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`\n35\t  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`\n36\t  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-runbook.md`\n37\t  - `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-recovery-playbook.md`\n38\t- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy: `## Phase 11: Hardening`, `## Documentation Requirements`, `## Testing Requirements`, `## Storage Design` (event log compaction), `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`, `## Scope Leakage`.\n39\t- Shared standards: `coding.md`, `definition-of-done-checklist.md`.\n40\t\n41\t## Review procedure\n42\t\n43\t1. Open `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/` and confirm one module file per test family: `large_repo_tests.rs`, `concurrency_tests.rs`, `recovery_tests.rs`, `corruption_tests.rs`, `partial_index_tests.rs`, `workspace_boundary_tests.rs`, `migration_tests.rs`. Confirm `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs` exists.\n44\t2. Run every Phase 11 test command end-to-end:\n45\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::large_repo_tests -- --include-ignored`\n46\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::concurrency_tests -- --include-ignored`\n47\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::recovery_tests`\n48\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::corruption_tests`\n49\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::partial_index_tests`\n50\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::workspace_boundary_tests`\n51\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::migration_tests`\n52\t   - `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::mcp_compat_tests`\n53\t   - Capture pass/fail for each; any failure is a blocker.\n54\t3. Open `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/large_repo_results.json` and confirm it contains entries for every hot path on every fixture; cross-check against T80's documented fixture list.\n55\t4. Build the doc coverage matrix: list every item from spec §Documentation Requirements (eleven items), find the matching file produced by T85 (or, for the MCP contract reference, the T61 deliverable). Any unmapped item is a blocker.\n56\t5. Open every doc from T85 and T86 and grep for required headings (the verification commands cover `## Overview`, `## Migration steps`, `## Daily operations`, `## Recovery procedures`, `## Replay from snapshot`); spot-check that the body content fills the heading promise rather than being a stub.\n57\t6. Open the runbook and confirm the deploy sequence quoted matches `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy character-for-character: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`.\n58\t7. Open the recovery playbook and confirm the replay-from-snapshot procedure cross-links to the T82 test that proves it works.\n59\t8. Run `wc -l` on every Phase 11 artifact and confirm no file exceeds 800 lines per `coding.md`.\n60\t9. Grep all Phase 11 artifacts for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, and unjustified suppressions — each hit is a blocker.\n61\t10. Cross-check that the test families from spec §Testing Requirements are all present: storage migration, event append/replay, graph identity, parser, memory link, contradiction/supersession, stale verification, retrieval ranking golden, workflow golden, MCP schema, compact/full render, concurrency, large fixture performance, extension compile/UI smoke. The Phase 11 task set adds the hardening + migration + MCP compat coverage; earlier phases cover the remainder. Confirm every family has at least one passing test.\n62\t\n63\t## Required sections in the review output file\n64\t\n65\tThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n66\t\n67\t- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix for spec §Phase 11 deliverables (large-repo perf, concurrency, recovery, corrupted-event, partial-index, workspace-boundary, migration, MCP schema compatibility, documentation) and §Testing Requirements (every required test family). One row per deliverable, evidence column citing the artifact and the test/heading.\n68\t- `## Doc coverage matrix` — one row per required doc from spec §Documentation Requirements (eleven items). Columns: spec item, file delivered, file path, status PASS/PASS-WITH-CAVEATS/BLOCK, notes.\n69\t- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. `coding.md` hard limits: file lengths (`wc -l` table for every Phase 11 file), forbidden-token grep results, suppression audit, tests-as-documentation audit (naming convention on every test function).\n70\t- `## Hardening evidence` — for every Phase 11 test family, capture: command run, pass count, fail count, slow-test inclusion flag (`--include-ignored` for large_repo and concurrency), notable timings from `large_repo_results.json`, any P99 budget margin or breach.\n71\t- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks. Follow-up tasks must be opened in this build (do not defer outside).\n72\t- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n73\t\n74\t## Verification\n75\t\n76\t- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where downstream gates can read it.\n77\t- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms spec alignment is a dedicated section.\n78\t- `grep -q '## Doc coverage matrix' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms doc coverage matrix present.\n79\t- `grep -q '## Coding-standard alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms standards audit performed.\n80\t- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R87-hardening-docs.md` — confirms the review concludes with a binding verdict.\n81\t\n82\t## Definition of done\n83\t\n84\t- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n85\t- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n86\t- [ ] `## Hardening evidence` and `## Findings` are also present (not gated by tasks.json verification but required for completeness).\n87\t- [ ] Every Phase 11 test command was actually executed and the result captured under `## Hardening evidence`.\n88\t- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9386ce4e-bd54-46a3-84f6-f4abe7cd962a","uuid":"5f66b2f4-d5e7-4a90-9a56-d2b74d0a58b9","timestamp":"2026-05-17T20:30:31.336Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"t