_resolution` paths ≤ 130 µs P99 against a 2 ms budget.\n\n## Issues encountered\n\n### F1 (in-scope, fixed) — flaky log capture in `corruption_tests`\n\n`test_truncated_event_log_file_reports_recovery_or_sqlite_error_without_panic` failed intermittently (~30–50% under parallel test execution; 0% with `--test-threads=1`) because `tracing`'s per-callsite Interest cache is keyed against the global subscriber, but `capture_logs` was installing a thread-local subscriber via `set_default`. Once another test's `tracing_subscriber::fmt::try_init()` installed a global default, the `info!` callsites in `EventStore::open` cached `Interest::Never` for the thread-local capture path. Rewrote `capture_logs` to use a process-wide global subscriber (installed once via `OnceLock`) that routes through a `ThreadLocalWriter`, restoring deterministic capture. 10/10 verification passes after fix; full hardening suite 43/43 pass.\n\n### F2 (out of R87 scope) — pre-existing unrelated failures in other phases\n\nThe broader `cargo test -p lattice-core --lib` run surfaced four failures unrelated to Phase 11:\n\n- `consolidation::deterministic_tests::duplicate_detector_emits_supersession_proposal` — passes in isolation; suggests Phase 6 test-ordering interference.\n- `consolidation::deterministic_tests::scanners_route_through_runtime_without_direct_writes`\n- `consolidation::session_tests::session_consolidation_hot_path_stays_under_five_milliseconds_p99`\n- `events::tests::every_payload_serializes_deterministically` — payload fixture missing `post_apply_state_hash` field that was added to `MemoryConsolidated` payload.\n\nThese belong to R18 (events) / R47 (consolidation) and are flagged in the R87 review's Findings (F2) for R88 (definition-of-done) to track. They are not Phase 11 hardening regressions and do not block R87.\n\n## Final status\n\n**complete.** Verdict: **PASS** (no follow-up tasks required).\n\n- Every Phase 11 test family runs green (43/43 hardening + 6/6 MCP compat).\n- Every 